      "answer": "Terence Tao discusses how AI can assist in solving hard math problems by filling in gaps and proposing new ideas, but also notes that AI struggles with knowing when it has made a wrong turn and can produce flawed proofs that look superficially flawless. He mentions that there are efforts to have an AI math olympiad where AIs will be given the same problems as human contestants and the outputs will have to be graded by the same judges.",
