      "query": "What does Pavel Durov say about Telegram and government censorship?",
      "type": "named_guest",
      "has_answer": true,
      "answer": "Pavel Durov says that Telegram has been fighting harmful content on its platform since 10 years ago and has daily transparency reports on how many channels related to child abuse or terrorist activity are blocked. He also mentions that Telegram has never shared a single private message with anyone, including governments and intelligence services, and that the company's design is such that no single government or entity can access user data. Additionally, Durov notes that Telegram is very protective of the private messages of users and that employees never can access private messages. He also talks about the pressure from governments, such as Russia and Iran, to ban Telegram and how the company has resisted this pressure.",
